    "degree_effect": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Structure extracted from one degree of success's text. A degree is a string field on its parent ability, so anything modelled about it lives here rather than on the degree itself. Deliberately extensible: `damage` is the only structured key today. saving_throw and skill_check wait on PFSRD2-Parser-2cby, because well under half the DCs that appear in degree text are saving throws at all -- most are Escape DCs or flat checks -- so typing a degree's DC as save_dc would claim something the source did not say. (The exact census lives on that ticket rather than here: it is measured from the corpus and moves whenever extraction changes, and a figure frozen into ten published descriptions has now gone stale twice.) `damage` is a CONSERVATIVE reading of the degree's text, not a complete one. Dice are omitted when the degree states them but they are not what it deals: an alternative (\"2d6 ... or 6d6 if legendary\" keeps only the base), Hit Points regained, dice carrying their own nested save, a per-unit rate rather than an amount, and a short list of degrees named in the parser where the damage lands on someone other than the degree's subject. Flat and splash damage are never extracted at all (PFSRD2-Parser-a1p7), and scaling stated inside a degree gives the base case only (PFSRD2-Parser-bsw3). So an absent entry means no DICE THIS DEGREE DEALS, not no damage, and a present entry is a floor rather than a total.",
      "properties": {
        "damage": {
          "additionalItems": false,
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/attack_damage"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "degree": {
          "enum": [
            "critical_success",
            "success",
            "failure",
            "critical_failure"
          ]
        },
        "subtype": {
          "enum": [
            "degree_effect"
          ]
        },
        "type": {
          "enum": [
            "stat_block_section"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "subtype",
        "degree"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
